\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces What the per-case agent does, case by case (30 outbreaks; three training seeds for each agent). Left and center: tests per case and accuracy by the clinician's label. The Rio-trained agent (blue) behaves like the clinician-guided rule (gray) for suspects labeled dengue or chikungunya and concludes suspects labeled non-arboviral without testing. Right: probability of a second test after a negative first result, for suspects labeled dengue or chikungunya. The idealized-geography agent (green), for which location is informative, tests far less and skips most second tests.}}{17}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
